ctx, md, v, mapped); fired { return d, true }\n    if d, fired := g.checkBelowHigh(ctx, md, v); fired { return d, true }\n    return Decision{}, false\n}\n```\n\nHmm checkService returning mapped value plus decision. Let me make `resolveService` helper returns (mapped string, decision Decision, fired bool). Or store mapped in a local: \n\n```go\nmapped, ok := g.lookupService(v.Service)\nif !ok { return needsInput(...), true }\nif mapped != v.Repo { ... }\n```\n\nDo it inline in check with small helpers:\n```go\nif d, fired := g.checkService(ctx, md, v); fired { return d, true }\n```\nand checkRepo re-lookups. Lookup is cheap; duplicate lookup is fine. Simpler. But rule i needs mapped repo; do lookup again in checkRepo. Fine.\n\nActually cleaner: checkService does both h and i? But requirement says one helper per rule. Keep separate; checkRepo does its own lookup.\n\ncheckHeading needs ctx for errors.Errorf.\n\nNow `checkParseOutcome`: rule a. The newline check only for five scalar fields. For a field present with newline. Use `strings.Contains(v, \"\\n\")`.\n\nRule d required fields = VerdictFieldOrder minus confidence:\n```go\nvar requiredFields = []string{FieldDefectID, FieldService, FieldRepo, FieldFileLine, FieldRootCause, FieldRecommendedFix, FieldEvidence}\n```\n\nNote: rule d checks missing or empty. But for `file:line` with Medium/Low empty, rule c already fired. Good.\n\nRule e: `checkFileLine` uses parseFileLine from lineguard.go. If !ok → failed message exact.\n\nRule g: `md.Frontmatter.String(FieldDefectID)`.\n\nNow `Evaluate` and `Review`.\n\nPotential issue: rule j when confidence Medium/Low and line present: `CheckLineGuard`. cloneRoot from gate. Good.\n\nLet me write it.","signature":"llm-proxy"}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8694a5b0-97a0-445