nt 10 says \"Where a row is about what the operator finally reads, additionally run the real delivery.NewPassthroughContentGenerator() ... and assert on the generated document\". So for passing row, run the generator with AgentResultInfo{Status: Done, NextPhase: \"done\", Output: marshaled} and assert the generated doc has phase: done.\n\nLet me implement a helper `deliver(ctx, originalContent, result) string` using the passthrough generator:\n```go\nfunc deliverDocument(ctx context.Context, result agentlib.AgentResultInfo) string {\n    generator := delivery.NewPassthroughContentGenerator()\n    doc, err := generator.Generate(ctx, \"\", result)\n    Expect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n    return doc\n}\n```\nNote Generate ignores originalContent for passthrough. result.Output must be marshaled md.\n\nFor failed/needs_input delivered body, the generator splices `## Failure` with the message in a fence. Requirement 10 says assert on generated doc including the fence. I'll do this for model passthrough tests and the ai_review failing rows maybe.\n\nFor ai_review failing rows, requirement 11: assert reason phrase in prefixed message and `## Verdict` count 0 on marshaled doc, plus evidence lines. The prefixed message is result.Message (contains \"> \"). Good.\n\nNow `phase: done` assertion: generated doc from passthrough with Status Done NextPhase done → applyStatusFrontmatter sets phase done, status completed. Assert `phase: done`.\n\nNow write lineguard_test.go.\n\nAlso direct CheckLineGuard for \"file absent\", \"beyond EOF\", \"symlink file\", \"dir symlink\", \"passing\". These use ctx.\n\nLet me write.","signature":"llm-proxy"}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8694a5b0-97a0-4457-bb19-1fb31c30a82f","uuid":"789bab4a-7008-4c09-9cfc-0a68f8e302cb","timestamp":"2026-