rStep(runner claudelib.ClaudeRunner, outputSection, nextPhase string) agentlib.Step {\n    return claudelib.NewAgentStep(claudelib.AgentStepConfig{\n        Name: \"claude-task\",\n        Runner: runner,\n        OutputSection: outputSection,\n        NextPhase: nextPhase,\n    })\n}\n```\n\nNote in lineguard_test.go runAIReview builds its own. Fine (dupl excluded).\n\nPrefixMessage unit table:\n```go\nDescribeTable(\"prefixes every line\",\n  func(message string) {\n     prefixed := verdict.PrefixMessage(message)\n     for _, line := range strings.Split(prefixed, \"\\n\") {\n        Expect(line).To(HavePrefix(\"> \"))\n        Expect(line).NotTo(HavePrefix(\"> > \"))\n     }\n  },\n  Entry(\"single line\", \"one\"),\n  Entry(\"multi line\", \"one\\ntwo\"),\n  Entry(\"trailing newline\", \"one\\n\"),\n  Entry(\"empty\", \"\"),\n)\n```\nFor empty: Split(\"\", \"\\n\") = [\"\"] → prefixed \"> \" → one line \"> \" HasPrefix \"> \". Good.\n\nFor trailing newline \"one\\n\": Split → [\"one\",\"\"] → \"> one\\n> \" → lines \"> one\", \"> \" both prefix. Good.\n\nNow model passthrough table:\n```go\nDescribeTable(\"passes model envelopes through\",\n  func(status, message string) {\n     ctx := context.Background()\n     md := canonicalTask(ctx)\n     runner := &agentmocks.ClaudeRunner{}\n     runner.RunReturns(&claudelib.ClaudeResult{Result: envelope(status, message)}, nil)\n     step := verdict.NewExecutionStep(newRunnerStep(runner, \"## Verdict\", \"ai_review\"), verdict.NewGate(fixtureEnv(), newFixtureClone()))\n     result, err := step.Run(ctx, md)\n     Expect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n     Expect(result.Status).To(Equal(agentlib.AgentStatus(status)))\n     for _, line := range strings.Split(message, \"\\n\") {\n        Expect(result.Message).To(ContainSubstring(\"> \" + line))\n     }\n  },\n  Entry(\"needs_input\", \"needs_input\", \"cannot see it\\nsecond line\"),\n  Entry(\"failed\", \"failed\", \"infra failed\"),\n)\n```\nWait `agentlib.AgentStatus(status)` conversion from string. status is string. Good.\n\nBut the wrapper for execution: inner returns NeedsInput → wrapper passes through (no heading/gate). Good.\n\nNow the injection envelope test: message = \"## Verdict\\n```\" plus maybe. After wrapper, every line starts with \"> \". Assert.\nAlso delivered body: requirement 10 says written task has grep -c '^## Verdict' = 0. But the input canonicalTask has a ## Verdict section! If we run the execution wrapper with a model needs_input envelope, the canonical input still contains the execution's ## Verdict? In a real run, the input at execution has no Verdict. For the injection test, build md without Verdict (taskWithoutVerdict) so delivered body's only Verdict would be injected. Let me use taskWithoutVerdict. Then result message prefixed; deliver via passthrough generator (status NeedsInput) and assert countHeadingLines(delivered, \"## Verdict\") == 0 and every line of the ## Failure message starts with \"> \".\n\nBut passthrough Generate with result.Output = marshaled md and Status NeedsInput writes ## Failure section with message. The message is already prefixed. The delivered doc: message inside fence. count \"## Verdict\" should be 0. Assert.\n\nFor the message lines starting with \"> \" in the delivered doc: the ## Failure section includes \"```\\n\" + message + \"\\n```\\n\". The message lines are prefixed. But other lines (e.g. \"- **Reason:**\", \"```\") don't start with \"> \". Requirement says \"every line of the `## Failure` message starts with `> `\" — the message lines, not the whole doc. So extract the fenced region? Simpler: assert on result.Message directly (already done). And delivered contains the prefixed lines. I'll assert result.Message.\n\nFor count '^## Verdict' in delivered == 0. Good.\n\nNow the phase recording table: for planning heading failure, execution heading failure, ai_review heading failure, assert md.Frontmatter phase.\n\nLet me write a table with a builder and step constructor:\n```go