{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a06c18a10c628a53","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Changelog\n2\t\n3\tAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n4\t\n5\tPlease choose versions by [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).\n6\t\n7\t* MAJOR version when you make incompatible API changes,\n8\t* MINOR version when you add functionality in a backwards-compatible manner, and\n9\t* PATCH version when you make backwards-compatible bug fixes.\n10\t\n11\t## Unreleased\n12\t\n13\t- feat: Add `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the fourth read-only observation script, cloning a public GitHub repo into the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` and reporting `clone_path`, `head_sha` and `default_branch` [rejects any reference that is not `owner/name`, resolves the destination with symlinks followed and refuses anything outside `repos/` before git runs or the filesystem is touched, then makes the clone non-writable]\n14\t- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]\n15\t\n16\t## v0.2.2\n17\t\n18\t- chore: remove orphaned section comments left in `.trivyignore` by the stale-ignore sweep\n19\t\n20\t## v0.2.1\n21\t\n22\t- chore: remove 9 stale vulnerability ignores (withdrawn advisory, module absent from go.mod, or version outside the affected range)\n23\t- chore: install Trivy from a pinned release tarball in CI so the job no longer depends on the retired apt-key helper\n24\t\n25\t## v0.2.0\n26\t\n27\t- feat: add a `check-task-link` gate that fails a PR whose body carries no `Task: <task_identifier>` line, and install Trivy from the upstream script so `test` stops failing on the retired keyring helper\n28\t\n29\t## v0.1.5\n30\t\n31\t- chore: bump `ERRCHECK_VERSION` to v1.30.0 and `GOSEC_VERSION` to v2.30.0. The pinned versions could not type-check the Go 1.27 stdlib, and these stay in step with the canonical `tools.env`.\n32\t\n33\t## v0.1.4\n34\t\n35\t- chore: update Go to 1.27.4 and github.com/bborbe/agent to v0.141.1, github.com/bborbe/cqrs to v0.6.16, github.com/bborbe/errors to v1.6.7, github.com/bborbe/kafka to v1.29.14, github.com/bborbe/sentry to v1.10.8, github.com/bborbe/service to v1.11.4, github.com/bborbe/time to v1.27.28, github.com/bborbe/vault-cli to v0.192.4\n36\t\n37\t## v0.1.3\n38\t\n39\t- chore: restate the do-not-merge contract in the gate workflow\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8694a5b0-97a0-4457-bb19-1fb31c30a82f","uuid":"c6a7e409-e209-46ed-b937-170c698b0e1a","timestamp":"2026-11-26T18:53:38.282Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/CHANGELOG.md","content":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nPlease choose versions by [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).\n\n* MAJOR version when you make incompatible API changes,\n* MINOR version when you add functionality in a backwards-compatible manner, and\n* PATCH version when you make backwards-compatible bug fixes.\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- feat: Add `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the fourth read-only observation script, cloning a public GitHub repo into the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` and reporting `clone_path`, `head_sha` and `default_branch` [rejects any reference that is not `owner/name`, resolves the destination with symlinks followed and refuses anything outside `repos/` before git runs or the filesystem is touched, then makes the clone non-writable]\n- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]\n\n## v0.2.2\n\n- chore: remove orphaned section comments left in `.trivyignore` by the stale-ignore sweep\n\n## v0.2.1\n\n- chore: remove 9 stale vulnerability ignores (withdrawn advisory, module absent from go.mod, or version outside the affected range)\n- chore: install Trivy from a pinned release tarball in CI so the job no longer depends on the retired apt-key helper\n\n## v0.2.0\n\n- feat: add a `check-task-link` gate that fails a PR whose body carries no `Task: <task_identifier>` line, and install Trivy from the upstream script so `test` stops failing on the retired keyring helper\n\n## v0.1.5\n\n- chore: bump `ERRCHECK_VERSION` to v1.30.0 and `GOSEC_VERSION` to v2.30.0. The pinned versions could not type-check the Go 1.27 stdlib, and these stay in step with the canonical `tools.env`.\n\n## v0.1.4\n\n- chore: update Go to 1.27.4 and github.com/bborbe/agent to v0.141.1, github.com/bborbe/cqrs to v0.6.16, github.com/bborbe/errors to v1.6.7, github.com/bborbe/kafka to v1.29.14, github.com/bborbe/sentry to v1.10.8, github.com/bborbe/service to v1.11.4, github.com/bborbe/time to v1.27.28, github.com/bborbe/vault-cli to v0.192.4\n\n## v0.1.3\n\n- chore: restate the do-not-merge contract in the gate workflow\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}}}
